--TEST--
an `extend` block cannot add a method named like a member of a compiler-declared interface, because Novis calls those by name: `compareTo`, `toString`, `iterate` and a static `parse` are each `E1012` — `rule:classes/an-extend-block-adds-members-to-a-type`
--FILE--
<?nvs
use Core\Time\Date;
use Core\Audience;

extend Date as Ordering {
    public function compareTo(Date $other): int {
        return 0;
    }

    public function toString(): string {
        return "a date";
    }
}

extend Audience as Audiences {
    public function iterate(): array<string> {
        return [];
    }

    public static function parse(string $s): Audience {
        return Audience::Public;
    }
}

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E1012]: an `extend` block cannot add a method named `compareTo`
  --> %s:6:21
  |
6 |     public function compareTo(Date $other): int {
  |                     ^^^^^^^^^ `compareTo` is a method of `Comparable`
  = help: give the method a different name. Novis calls `compareTo` by its name, and it never calls an added method that way. To give a class of your own this method, write `implements Comparable`

error[E1012]: an `extend` block cannot add a method named `toString`
%A
error[E1012]: an `extend` block cannot add a method named `iterate`
%A
error[E1012]: an `extend` block cannot add a method named `parse`
%A
error: aborting due to 4 errors
%A
